# Read by supercronic inside deploy/journal.Dockerfile's image.
#
# Same TZ convention as deploy/crontab (see that file's header) — not
# because this job is market-hours sensitive, but so both crontabs read
# the same way and a human checking "did this run today" doesn't have to
# convert timezones in their head.
CRON_TZ=America/New_York

# Nightly, every day (not just weekdays): the Sunday `weekly` job and the
# Wednesday `momls2x` job both write reports too, and this is simpler than
# trying to track which days the engine might have written something.
# journal-commit.sh is a no-op (skip-if-clean) if there's nothing to
# commit. 23:00 ET is comfortably after every engine job in deploy/crontab.
0 23 * * * /usr/local/bin/journal-commit
